    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [X] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [X] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n- [X] I have updated 'mini.nvim' to latest version\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.files\n\n### Description\n\nWhen I open mini.files I get the following \"no glyph\" icon for each item in the menu \r\n\r\n![Screenshot 2024-11-10 at 11 38 39](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/f522867d-584b-4ffd-b015-fbe26d24a455)\r\n\r\n**is it possible to disable this?**\r\n\n\n### Neovim version\n\nNVIM v0.10.2\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n1. use [berkeley mono typeface](https://berkeleygraphics.com/typefaces/berkeley-mono/)\r\n2. open mini.files\r\n3. see issue\r\n\n\n### Expected behavior\n\nNo glyphs shown, similar to oil.nvim\n\n### Actual behavior\n\nNo glyph icon shown",
