            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "For future reference, making 'mini.files' to not show icons can be done by [supplying custom `config.content.prefix` function](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/998cfcf1fdd0a6830d0fc35f1c054a6f55de1e7f/doc/mini-files.txt#L443).\r\n\r\nAt the same time, judging by the screenshot, icons are provided by 'mini.icons'. In this case the better approach might be to use ['ascii' style when setting up 'mini.icons'](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/998cfcf1fdd0a6830d0fc35f1c054a6f55de1e7f/doc/mini-icons.txt#L190). But the best approach is to set up terminal emulator to have a \"fallback\" font just for this types of glyphs (for example, [`NerdFontsSymbolsOnly`](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/998cfcf1fdd0a6830d0fc35f1c054a6f55de1e7f/doc/mini-icons.txt#L61-L63)).",
